      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. Let me write an improved, more understandable version.\n\nThe test constructs a `JsonTypeInfo.Value` with a `null` id type and `Boolean.FALSE` for both `requireTypeIdForSubtypes` and `writeTypeIdForDefaultImpl`, then verifies:\n1. `isEnabled()` returns `false` (because `_idType` is null)\n2. `getIdVisible()` returns `false`\n3. `shouldWriteTypeIdForDefaultImpl()` returns `false` (because `_writeTypeIdForDefaultImpl` is `Boolean.FALSE`)The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version uses meaningful variable names (`inclusionType`, `defaultImpl`, `falseFlag`, `value`, `enabled`) and adds inline comments and a Javadoc explaining what the test verifies, making it much easier for developers to understand the intent without tracing through auto-generated identifiers."
    }
